---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-10-02T00:00:00Z');
---

<BaseLayout title="Now" description="What Eric Hare is working on right now, updated periodically.">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Now"
    title="What I'm focused on right now."
    lede="A page in the spirit of Derek Sivers' nownownow.com. A snapshot, not a résumé."
  />

  <Section>
    <div class="prose-styled">
      <p>
        <em>Updated {lastUpdated.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })} from Lake Stevens, WA.</em>
      </p>

      <h2>JEStats</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Consulting and creative work.</strong> Growing
          <a href="https://jestats.io/">JEStats (J&amp;E Consulting)</a>, the studio I run with my
          partner in Lake Stevens. We help with data analysis, website design and management,
          print and social graphics, and AI integrations. Projects start with a written scope.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Astra DB Plugin.</strong> Building a community integration that helps coding
          agents inspect live schemas, search data, and work with Astra DB through guarded tools.
          <a href="/projects/astra-db-plugin">Project notes</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SkillRoute.</strong> Helping agents find relevant skills with ranked matches,
          confidence scores, and source evidence. A local-first tool for skill discovery and routing.
          <a href="/projects/skillroute">Project notes</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Codebase Mentor.</strong> Helping developers understand unfamiliar repositories
          with architecture answers, change plans, and onboarding guides grounded in source code.
          <a href="/projects/codebase-mentor">Project notes</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Langflow, IBM.</strong> Core maintainer. Current focus: MCP reliability and security,
          the Langflow SDK and release workflow, model-provider consistency, and production developer
          experience.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI Workbench.</strong> Building the
          <a href="/projects/ai-workbench">self-hosted Astra workbench</a> for retrieval-backed
          applications: knowledge bases, ingest, retrieval experiments, agents, MCP, and runtime
          operations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Developer and Operator Experience team.</strong> Making Langflow easier to run in
          production and easier to hack on in development — the two usually want different things.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Side projects</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Verity.</strong> My main project outside of work: an open, domain-general engine
          for forensic surface comparison — calibrated likelihood ratios, not black-box "matches,"
          from 3-D scans of bullets, cartridge cases, and toolmarks.
          <a href="/projects/verity">Project notes</a> ·
          <a href="https://verity.codes">verity.codes</a> ·
          <a href="https://github.com/erichare/verity">source</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Aeroza.</strong> Open-source weather infrastructure for live radar, geospatial
          queries, streaming APIs, nowcasting, and forecast verification.
          <a href="/projects/aeroza">Project notes</a> ·
          <a href="https://github.com/erichare/aeroza">source</a>.
        </li>
        <li>Turning this site into a more visual, evidence-first record of the work.</li>
        <li>Occasional pushes to <a href="https://github.com/erichare/bulletxtrctr">bulletxtrctr</a> and the CSAFE bullet-matching pipeline.</li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/OmniacsDAO">OmniacsDAO</a> — Numerai tooling,
          <code>experiment-builder</code>, <code>letter-loops</code>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Reading & learning</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Papers on agent tool-use evaluation and MCP security boundaries.</li>
        <li>Rust, no longer for no good reason — Verity's X3P codec is written in it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Not doing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Conference travel (remote-first for 2026).</li>
        <li>Unscoped projects. A written scope helps me give studio work and the day job at IBM the attention they need.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
